{
  "content": {
    "arguments": "$ARGUMENTS",
    "constraints": [
      {
        "id": "0ce1219d-0350-4c20-888b-af23d58e31bc",
        "text": "Use the Bash tool. The Pebbles CLI at \"{PEBBLES_CLI}\" is the ONLY sanctioned way to change spec files — never edit .pebble files directly."
      },
      {
        "id": "8b12bef4-c08b-4fbe-8515-51d862d4468d",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Spec mutation contract (rules/system/spec-mutation-contract)"
      },
      {
        "id": "c99301c5-4d3e-4e19-8892-dd4dd8acf815",
        "text": "Bound by system rule: Analysis standard (rules/system/analysis-standard)"
      }
    ],
    "examples": [],
    "kind": "skill",
    "onFailure": [
      {
        "id": "22a8ca8c-6d85-4447-bdf3-43d85478657b",
        "text": "Read the CLI error — it names the fix; correct the call and retry once"
      },
      {
        "id": "e90c2c57-d7c4-4624-bdab-0a3ed3b57466",
        "text": "NEVER fall back to editing .pebble files directly, whatever failed"
      },
      {
        "id": "b47d09a8-0f0a-4627-8db4-90c8dad57f93",
        "text": "If still blocked, report the exact command and error to the user and stop"
      }
    ],
    "output": "A Discovery Brief: restated intent (+alternatives), READY vs GAPS (each gap with why it matters and what would fill it), and the exact recommended next skill/agent with arguments. Strictly read-only.",
    "prerequisites": [
      {
        "id": "bf4c1944-59df-4537-8047-7854558990ee",
        "text": "A saved map (relay reports its age; map --fresh if stale) — readiness is judged against it"
      }
    ],
    "purpose": "Discover: understand the ticket/context + whether the spec is ready, before any work",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "031e9864-8965-4fb7-a36f-0ae2cb3aa3b7",
        "text": "Discover — understand what the user actually wants and the context (the ticket/problem), before anything acts: $ARGUMENTS"
      },
      {
        "id": "4cb1aa90-e491-457c-a3db-3a7067ac1ad1",
        "text": "This skill is STRICTLY READ-ONLY — no create/update/set-status/add-finding, no code changes. It exists so nothing downstream runs on assumptions."
      },
      {
        "id": "67f2b187-3eed-4e83-839e-9181b0891317",
        "text": "STEP 1 — RESTATE THE ASK: goal, scope, success criteria, and the interpretation you chose — with the plausible alternatives named. If interpretations genuinely diverge, ask (max 5 targeted questions); never pick silently."
      },
      {
        "id": "01cf484c-e381-4b34-af18-eafe06a5923b",
        "text": "STEP 2 — READINESS CHECK on the target pebble(s): `get` them and `refs` them. Assess against what the INTENDED work needs: is the description real (not filler)? do units (fields/items/nodes) carry descriptions + statuses? do refs resolve and cover the load-bearing relationships (FKs, subprocess links, governing rules)? are codeLinks present and in the map? is the map fresh enough for the task?"
      },
      {
        "id": "1713d9c6-d17b-4fe3-8233-27198693c420",
        "text": "STEP 3 — THE DISCOVERY BRIEF (your output): (a) the restated intent; (b) READY: what the spec already provides; (c) GAPS: each missing piece, WHY it matters for this specific task, and what information from the user would fill it; (d) RECOMMENDED NEXT STEP: the exact skill (+agent) to run once settled — shallow/deep/regular extract, fix, verify, plan… — with the arguments to pass."
      },
      {
        "id": "3bf19d34-fc66-46b9-8c84-1f34a8bc6274",
        "text": "Do NOT fix the gaps yourself — surfacing them is the job; the user decides. When everything is settled, the user triggers the follow-up skill."
      }
    ],
    "verify": [
      {
        "id": "d9c444fe-c447-4082-a3a6-3c147aa07b3c",
        "text": "NOTHING was written — no pebble create/update/status, no finding, no code"
      },
      {
        "id": "21d9ca66-822d-406b-81a2-6135d9751d5f",
        "text": "The brief contains: restated intent with alternatives, READY list, GAPS each with why-it-matters, and a concrete recommended next step"
      },
      {
        "id": "66253ff1-7866-46bc-81f3-9b50a0df0c92",
        "text": "Genuinely diverging interpretations were asked about, not silently chosen"
      }
    ],
    "whenToUse": "FIRST, before extraction/implementation/anything — settle what the user wants and whether the spec is ready for it. Also the place to discuss and refine intent until everything is settled; downstream skills then run without assumptions."
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-21T14:32:38.730Z",
